  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\vec{a}=\\hat{j}-\\hat{k}$ and $\\vec{c}=\\hat{i}-\\hat{j}-\\hat{k}$. Then vector $\\vec{b}$ satisfying $\\vec{a} \\times \\vec{b}+\\vec{c}=\\overrightarrow{0}$ and $\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b}=3$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "aaSJI",
      "text": "\n$2 \\hat{i}-\\hat{j}+2 \\hat{k}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "j5zfI",
      "text": "\n$\\hat{i}-\\hat{j}-2 \\hat{k}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "CFLEw",
      "text": "\n$\\hat{i}+\\hat{j}-2 \\hat{k}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AWDqX",
      "text": "\n$-\\hat{i}+\\hat{j}-2 \\hat{k}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{c}}=\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{b}} \\times \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{b}} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{c}}=0$\n$\\Rightarrow\\left(\\mathrm{b}_1 \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+\\mathrm{b}_2 \\hat{j}+\\mathrm{b}_3 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}}\\right) \\cdot(\\hat{\\mathrm{i}}-\\hat{\\mathrm{j}}-\\hat{\\mathrm{k}})=0$\n$\\mathrm{~b}_1-\\mathrm{b}_2-\\mathrm{b}_3=0$\nand $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{b}}=3$\n$\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{b}_2-\\mathrm{b}_3=3$\n$\\mathrm{~b}_1=\\mathrm{b}_2+\\mathrm{b}_3=3+2 \\mathrm{~b}_3$\n$\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{b}}=\\left(3+2 \\mathrm{~b}_3\\right) \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+\\left(3+\\mathrm{b}_3\\right) \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}+\\mathrm{b}_3 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}}$",
    "image": null
  },
